  "caveats": [
    "one-vs-rest binaries replace the multiclass model after a documented scale collapse (2.26M rows, in-sample scan recall 0.00 unweighted and 0.02/0.00 with capped weights via both sklearn mechanisms; same code learns scan at 0.99 on a 400k subsample), binary objective is stable at all tested scales",
    "infiltration excluded from the ensemble: 29 flows corpus-wide cannot be trained or evaluated honestly",
    "protocol A shares window context across neighbouring flows (mild leakage); protocol B (LOSO) is the strict cross-day number for ddos: the ROC-AUC transfers (0.92-0.997) while absolute thresholds do not (in-sample scores saturate at 1.0) ,  the oracle operating point is a labelled diagnostic, and deployment requires per-deployment calibration",
    "bot/webattack thresholds are tuned on ~1-2k positives; treat their absolute numbers as indicative, bot coverage relies primarily on the dedicated beacon/TLS detectors; a class whose tuning slice cannot reach precision>=0.5 has its alerting channel disabled rather than shipping a junk operating point"
  ]
